# Remaining implementation work · `plan:nrz:backlog`

## LC closing work · `sec:nrz:backlog-lc-closing`

**Convention (The register decides completion; the backlog orders work)** · `conv:nrz:backlog-standing`

The completion authority is (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`), under (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-completion`). Each implementation item in (`sec:nrz:backlog-lc-closing`) corresponds to one open or partial closing claim at (`obs:nrz:lc-closing-baseline`), cites its governing design and states the evidence needed to meet it. Status changes are recorded in the register and the corresponding backlog item is removed or revised in the same change, so this ordering cannot imply a different standing. Met claims, follow-ons and work outside LC are excluded from that section. Sections outside LC carry their own standing and do not imply an LC completion claim. The final review item enforces (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-independent-review`) after all claims are met; labelled blocking review findings become or update backlog items with consistent register standing. This document orders implementation and review dependencies; it does not declare another completion authority.

**Rule (LC dependency order)** · `rule:nrz:backlog-lc-order`

The engine tile/mask surface, enclosed kernels, exact cache, reusable lowerings, bounded graph walk precede LC family authority and indexed lowering. The relation items supply the original semantics that those lowerings must preserve. LC lowerings and complete plan integration precede standing streams and their lifecycle acceptance; owner aggregation, route-complete observation and fresh-process evidence precede the final scale measurement. Items sharing prerequisites can be developed independently, but their acceptance must include the complete dependency scope. The concept (`spec:nrz:lc-compute-concept`) and overhead-tracking design (`step:nrz:backlog-lc-overhead-design`) precede the implementations they govern; the theoretical model and predicted budget precede component tracking; the scale run supplies the final measurement attachment and the overhead-bound result. The independent closing review is last, after all claims including scale and the explained-overhead claims are met; no earlier component result supplies its verdict.

